  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_051: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, concat → acc 0.427), the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually provides a meaningful advantage over a unimodal baseline. config_018 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is the cleanest single-factor comparison: it is identical to config_051 except the image modality is removed. If RNA-only performs comparably (~0.42–0.44), the image contributes little and we should focus budget on RNA representation and profile/aggregation choices. If RNA-only is substantially lower, the image is a key signal and we should next explore image encoder variants (e.g., imagenet_vit_l). This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design decision (multimodal vs. unimodal) before committing further experiments to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

